# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
# Local docker-compose stack — secrets that used to be hard-coded (RunPod plan F9)
# Copy the relevant lines into the git-ignored .env files:
#   DVAS_Dashboard/.env   → KC_CLIENT_SECRET, ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET, DVAS_SERVICE_KEY, JWT_SECRET, ANALYTICS_SERVICE_KEY
#   dvas_ingest/.env      → KC_CLIENT_SECRET, ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET, KEYCLOAK_ADMIN_PASSWORD (already there)
# and dvas_ingest/ingest/scripts/users.local.json (format: users.example.json)
# Use the values your local Keycloak already has (Keycloak admin → Clients → Credentials).
# ════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
KC_CLIENT_SECRET=
ADMIN_CLIENT_SECRET=
DVAS_SERVICE_KEY=
JWT_SECRET=
ANALYTICS_SERVICE_KEY=
